    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters August 21st with **Corbin Carroll** serving as our undisputed anchor. With a robust 78.75 score, **Corbin Carroll** capitalizes on a prime matchup against Lodolo; the combination of a favorable park environment and a strong order position (#2) makes him our high-upside play for both R and SB. **Vinnie Pasquantino** (67.49) and **Isaac Paredes** (65.97) also provide high-floor stability against their respective right-handed counterparts. While **Gabriel Moreno** (65.11) faces a tough matchup in Lodolo, his specific platoon alignment and xwOBA efficiency suggest he is well-positioned to contribute value behind the dish.\n\nWe are navigating significant efficiency hurdles today, particularly with **Mickey Moniak** (53.27) and **Jose Caballero** (54.20). While **Jose Caballero** holds a +13% boost from his platoon advantage against Fluharty, he remains a volatile start due to the opposing pitcher\u2019s skill set. The tightest decision on the bench was **Griffin Conine** (45.13), whose elite xwOBA (0.396) and stolen base potential were ultimately sidelined by a difficult matchup against Lord and a lack of overall projected efficiency compared to our UTIL anchor, **Josh Naylor** (58.40). **Seiya Suzuki** remains a point of concern; with his lineup pending, we are relying on an assumed #2 slot, but his -5% park penalty and -4% SP skill adjustment mean he is on the bubble of being shifted if his batting order slips. Proceed with caution on **Cole Young** and **Max Muncy**, who sit at the lower end of our starting floor due to unfavorable order positions and elite opposing pitching adjustments.",
